    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here's the full ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without it, the request is denied (403) before any function runs.\n\n## In-order validations and side-effects\n\nThe pipeline runs 21 steps; steps 8 onward all run inside a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the end.\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 reads the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`).\n- *Side-effect:* normalizes `address` in place if present \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n- *Validation:* requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-null and non-blank (address checked *after* normalization). Any missing \u2192 **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing each offending field.\n- Publishes the validated body for later steps.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 only when a postcode is supplied (absent/blank is allowed).\n- *Validation:* must be exactly 4 digits; and if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown city region \u2192 any 4-digit value accepted. Otherwise \u2192 **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n**3. `ValidateRegistrationDate`** \u2014 only when `registrationDate` is supplied.\n- *Validation:* must not be later than the server's current date. Future date \u2192 **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n\n**4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n- *Side-effect:* rewrites `telephone` in place to E.164 form (strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps `+`/country code or assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`, requires 8\u201315 digits).\n- *Validation:* a value that can't form a valid E.164 number \u2192 **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 email is optional (null/blank left untouched).\n- *Validation:* when present must be syntactically valid \u2192 else **400** `InvalidEmailException`.\n- *Side-effect:* trims and lower-cases the stored `email`.\n\n**6. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 optional email only.\n- *Validation:* rejects domains on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n**7. `ResolveRegistrationDate`**\n- *Side-effect:* computes the effective registration date \u2014 supplied-or-today, rolled forward off Saturday/Sunday to the next Monday \u2014 and publishes it as a variable used by the daily-limit, bulk-warning, and default-date steps.\n\n**8. `EnsureCityCapacity`** *(transactional)*\n- *Validation:* counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); \u2265 50 \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`. (New owner not yet saved, so excluded.)\n\n**9. `EnsureDailyLimit`** *(transactional)*\n- *Validation:* counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the resolved business day; \u2265 100 \u2192 **429** `DailyLimitReachedException`.\n\n**10. `BuildOwner`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n**11. `AssignHousehold`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `householdId` = first 12 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`; `null` when no postcode.\n\n**12. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`** *(transactional)*\n- *Validation:* rejects **409** `DuplicateIdentityException` if (a) an existing owner shares the same `householdId` \u2014 unless the request set `sharesHousehold` \u2014 or (b) the new owner's whole `identityKey` (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) equals an existing owner's (always rejected, even for declared members).\n\n**13. `FlagPossibleDuplicate`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Skipped (false/null) when `sharesHousehold` or no postcode. Otherwise flags true and records the lowest-id existing owner sharing the same last name + postcode but a *different* telephone.\n\n**14. `AssignHouseholdSize`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners with the same `householdId` + 1; 1 when no household.\n\n**15. `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* writes the resolved business-day date onto the owner (overwriting any raw weekend date supplied).\n\n**16. `AssignCustomerCode`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode/city and HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n\n**17. `AssignNamesakeCount`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**18. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already exist on the resolved business day.\n\n**19. `SaveOwner`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n**20. `AuditOwnerCreated`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n\n**21. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(transactional)*\n- *Side-effect:* maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. Transaction commits.\n\n**Notes:**\n- Any thrown exception falls through to its handler YAML under `officefloor/escalation/`; anything unmatched falls through to Spring's advice. `DataIntegrityViolationException` at save time also has a handler.\n- All validations run *before* the write steps, so an invalid request never opens the transaction. The four \"409/429\" business checks (steps 8, 9, 12) and the duplicate flagging read the repository live within the transaction."
